Rem ==================================================================
Rem spiro-core.shoddy — the drawing, as a value.
Rem
Rem This half knows nothing about windows, turtles, or pixels. It turns
Rem a step number into a Step record — how far to draw, how far to turn
Rem afterwards, and what colour to use — so a whole picture is a
Rem List Of Step: ordinary data you can test without a screen.
Rem
Rem It includes nothing at all. Map, Range and Wrap are builtins, and
Rem keeping the geometry free of machines is what lets test.shoddy run
Rem anywhere, including a build server with no display.
Rem ==================================================================

Type Step
    Ahead As Number          Rem how far this step draws
    Turn  As Number          Rem degrees to turn when it lands
    Red   As Number
    Green As Number
    Blue  As Number

Rem Ninety-one degrees, not ninety. A square drawn with ninety closes
Rem and retraces itself forever; the extra degree makes each lap land
Rem slightly rotated from the last, and that near-miss is the spiral.
Def TurnAngle() As Number
    91

Rem How many steps the finished drawing takes.
Def DefaultSteps() As Number
    160

Rem Step i reaches a little further than step i-1 and sits on a slightly
Rem different colour. The three channels climb at different rates, so
Rem the hue drifts as the spiral opens; Wrap folds each one back inside
Rem 0..255 however far the counter runs — including below zero, which is
Rem where the blue channel starts heading almost immediately.
Def StepWith(i As Number, angle As Number) As Step
    Step(i * 2, angle, Wrap(i * 9, 256), Wrap(i * 5 + 90, 256), Wrap(300 - i * 4, 256))

Def StepAt(i As Number) As Step
    StepWith(i, TurnAngle())

Rem The whole picture, before anything is drawn: n steps in order. A
Rem bare name in argument position is passed as a function, not called,
Rem so this reads as "make a step for each number in 1..n".
Def Plan(n As Number) As List Of Step
    Map(Range(1, n), StepAt)

Rem The same plan at any angle you like — what spiro-keys.shoddy varies
Rem while the window is open. Plan is this with the angle fixed, which
Rem is the whole difference between a picture and a toy.
Def PlanWith(n As Number, angle As Number) As List Of Step
    Map(Range(1, n), Fn(i) => StepWith(i, angle))
